diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 8724fab..0ab34ba 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@ All notable changes to Packeteer are documented here. Versions are Git tags on `
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- Load-test RSS plateau and leak check (#112). The `pr` check read 379 MiB of growth after #110 (Actions run 37080504822) while peak RSS stayed under 6144; #120 set the budget at 384 and it stays there. The extra was the collector's return-and-refill on a taller heap, not an unbounded per-prefix map, and the heap is trimmed where that was cheap: one iBGP path per prefix is stored in the route entry instead of a map (710 to 358 bytes per prefix on a 50k synthetic table), `Lookup` and `Covering` skip prefix lengths with no selected route, per-address probe semaphores are dropped when the host leaves the probe set, the flow reader decodes in its socket buffer and reuses its observation slice and eviction scratch, and the fixed prober formats the target address only when a path matches on it. The load job also fails when RSS is still climbing at the end: new budget `rss_slope_mb` (192 for `pr`, 192 for the weekly soak) is the smaller of the Theil-Sen slope over the last third of the run times that third, and the last-sixth median minus the middle-third median. A soft `GOMEMLIMIT` was tried and dropped: on Actions run 38058605143 it pushed CPU to 2.6 cores and flow drops to 13.5 %. No budget is raised. Observe stays the default. Nothing is announced that is not in the learned RIB. Rollback: revert this change.
+
 - UI display bugs (#171). The header mode chip sets its own colors, so observe, suggest, and inject each meet WCAG AA (the observe chip had inherited the header's white text onto the light pill). On a custom dashboard the improvements widget is titled Recommended improvements outside inject and Active improvements in inject; a title the operator set on that widget is kept. Widget timestamps use the dashboard local format (`toLocaleString`), the same formatter as the main page. Each settings-form provider field (name, probe source, next hop, cost, commit) and the wizard's three provider fields have a visible label, and that label is the accessible name. The docker job's UI smoke covers the chip, the title, the labels, and the formatted time. No new config key. No announce-path change. Observe stays the default. The mode banner stays on the dashboard. Rollback: revert this change.
 
 - FRR HA lab lease-release check (#190). Step 7 grepped `docker compose logs` once for `ha: lease released`. The logging driver can deliver that line about a second after the process has written it (Actions run 37789070267), so a release that did happen failed the job. `lab/checklease` watches the lease file from inside the standby, armed before SIGTERM, and fails if pk-a does not release the record within 20s. The released flag is overwritten when the standby takes the lease, so the watch has to see that transition; a record that was already released does not count, and a release that never arrives still fails. The 10s takeover bound is unchanged. No config key. No announce-path change. Rollback: revert this change; the lab goes back to the one-shot log grep.
